A good e-commerce frontend starts with five core pages: **home, product listing, product details, cart, and checkout**. You can build these with React, then connect them to your product, inventory, and payment APIs.

Here’s a small React starting point with a responsive product grid and working cart count.

### 1. Create the project

```bash
npm create vite@latest my-store -- --template react
cd my-store
npm install
npm run dev
```

### 2. Add the storefront

Replace `src/App.jsx` with:

```jsx
import { useState } from "react";
import "./App.css";

const products = [
  { id: 1, name: "Canvas Tote", price: 24.99 },
  { id: 2, name: "Ceramic Mug", price: 18.0 },
  { id: 3, name: "Notebook", price: 12.5 },
];

const formatPrice = (price) =>
  new Intl.NumberFormat("en-US", {
    style: "currency",
    currency: "USD",
  }).format(price);

export default function App() {
  const [cart, setCart] = useState([]);

  function addToCart(product) {
    setCart((items) => [...items, product]);
  }

  const total = cart.reduce((sum, item) => sum + item.price, 0);

  return (
    <>
      <header className="header">
        <a href="/" className="logo">My Store</a>
        <span aria-live="polite">
          Cart: {cart.length} items · {formatPrice(total)}
        </span>
      </header>

      <main>
        <h1>Shop our products</h1>

        <div className="product-grid">
          {products.map((product) => (
            <article className="product-card" key={product.id}>
              <h2>{product.name}</h2>
              <p>{formatPrice(product.price)}</p>
              <button onClick={() => addToCart(product)}>
                Add {product.name} to cart
              </button>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
      </main>
    </>
  );
}
```

### 3. Add responsive styling

Replace `src/App.css` with:

```css
* {
  box-sizing: border-box;
}

body {
  margin: 0;
  font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
  color: #222;
  background: #f7f7f7;
}

.header {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 1rem;
  padding: 1rem 5%;
  background: white;
  border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd;
}

.logo {
  color: inherit;
  font-size: 1.25rem;
  font-weight: bold;
  text-decoration: none;
}

main {
  max-width: 1100px;
  margin: auto;
  padding: 2rem 5%;
}

.product-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));
  gap: 1rem;
}

.product-card {
  padding: 1.5rem;
  background: white;
  border: 1px solid #ddd;
  border-radius: 8px;
}

button {
  padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
  color: white;
  background: #222;
  border: 0;
  border-radius: 4px;
  cursor: pointer;
}

button:focus-visible,
a:focus-visible {
  outline: 3px solid #3975ff;
  outline-offset: 3px;
}
```

This is a **frontend prototype**: products are hardcoded, and the cart resets when the page reloads.

### Next steps

- Fetch products and images from your backend or commerce platform.
- Add search, filters, product detail pages, and a cart page.
- Persist the cart using an API or browser storage.
- Integrate a payment provider such as Stripe for checkout. Have your backend verify prices and inventory; never rely on frontend totals.
- Test on mobile and with keyboard and screen-reader navigation.

If you share your preferred stack and whether you already have a backend, I can tailor the implementation.
